Scroll a long output
Reveal cannot scroll for you, but a fragment can.


_scroll.html
Reveal.on('fragmentshown', (event) =&gt; {
  if (event.fragment.classList.contains("scroll")) {
    Reveal
      .getCurrentSlide()
      .querySelector(".cell-output code")
      .scrollTo({
        top: 1000,
        behavior: "smooth",
      })
  }
});








https://slidecrafting-book.com/fragments#scroll-output

And the way back
fragmenthidden is the same handler with top: 0.

_scroll.html
Reveal.on('fragmenthidden', (event) =&gt; {
  if (event.fragment.classList.contains("scroll")) {
    Reveal
      .getCurrentSlide()
      .querySelector(".cell-output code")
      .scrollTo({
        top: 0,
        behavior: "smooth",
      })
  }
});


Two numbers apart. That is what “the exact inverse” buys you.

